      // ── room_layouts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      // WHAT A ROOM SCAN LEAVES BEHIND (RoomPlan Phase 2, 2026-08-17).
      //
      // PARAMETERS, NEVER THE MESH. RoomPlan returns dimensioned surfaces and categorised objects; a
      // USDZ is an OUTPUT of those. Storing the mesh would freeze the drawing style on the day of the
      // scan, and only parameters can be re-rendered as something else later.
      //
      // ONE ROW PER ROOM, and the label is the homeowner's word. "Utility room" and "Mom's bathroom"
      // are both real, so this is free text for the same reason home_items.room is.
      //
      // The payload is JSON rather than columns because nothing queries INTO a layout — it is rendered
      // whole or not at all. Columns would be a schema to migrate for no lookup anybody performs.
      //
      // synced_at IS NULL UNTIL THE IMAGE CONSENT GRANT SAYS OTHERWISE. A layout is image-class data
      // (ruling 2026-08-17): it describes the interior of somebody's home, which is far closer to a
      // photograph of the utility room than to a model number, and somebody who declined to share
